# The build context is the whole repository, because the server depends on nine
# path crates and a context narrowed to its own directory cannot see them. What
# it does not need is everything below — which is most of the bytes, and all of
# the ones that would invalidate the layer cache on every edit.
target/
fuzz/target/
# Agent scratch space, and it is not small: a finished worktree keeps its own
# full `target/` tree, so this directory reached 4.4 GB and every `docker build`
# was shipping all of it as context — which failed outright on one machine
# rather than merely being slow. `target/` above does not cover it, because
# these are *nested* copies under a different prefix. It is also working state
# that has no business in a layer.
.claude/
webapp/pkg/
tests/browser/node_modules/
tests/browser/test-results/
sdk/*/node_modules/
.git/
docs/
*.png
# Never: this holds the signing secret, and anything in the context can end up
# in a layer. The compose file passes it as an environment variable instead.
.env
.env.*
